        "term": "Idempotency",
        "pronunciation": "eye-dem-POH-ten-see",
        "definition": "Applying the operation multiple times yields the same result as applying it once.",
        "analogy": "Like pressing an elevator call button repeatedly.",
        "contextualExample": "PUT /users/42 with the same body is idempotent; POST /users is not.",
        "doNotConfuseWith": [
          { "label": "Pure functions",   "why": "Pure functions have no side effects." },
          { "label": "Atomic operations","why": "Atomicity is all-or-nothing; idempotency is repeatability." }
